  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/vkhorikov/Nitpick",
  "published": "2026-11-14T21:16:09.01Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First release.\n\n- **Only formatting is on.** Nitpick turns rules on one at a time, and none of Microsoft's code-analysis (CA) or code-style (IDE) rules is on yet: the build sets `AnalysisMode=None`, and `.editorconfig` has no category-wide severity line such as `category-Style`. The build adds no warnings beyond the compiler's own. Later releases turn rules on; which ones is Nitpick's choice, with nothing to configure.\n- **Formatting:** `scripts/fix-and-verify.sh` formats the files a change touches (`dotnet format`, then ReSharper's `cleanupcode` with Nitpick's settings), then builds with warnings as errors. `--all` does the whole solution.\n- **NIT rules:** NIT1001 (don't end async method names with 'Async', with a fixer) is on. NIT2001, NIT2002, NIT3001, NIT3002 and NIT3003 are registered but don't detect anything yet.\n- **Install check (NIT9001):** the build fails when Nitpick's repo files (`.editorconfig`, `<solution>.DotSettings`, `scripts/fix-and-verify.sh`, the `jb` tool entry) are missing or differ from this version, and prints the command that syncs them.",
